<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ruicheng</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ruicheng County</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ruicheng is a county in the far south-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanxi">Shanxi</a>, on the north bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a>, in Yuncheng prefecture. It takes its name from the ancient State of Rui. It is known for the Yongle Palace, a Daoist temple complex with celebrated Yuan-dynasty wall paintings, moved there in 1959–1964 to make way for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanmenxia">Sanmenxia</a> reservoir.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ruicheng.jpg" alt="Ruicheng" width="320" height="239" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Underbar dk · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yongle_Palace_-_Chunyang_Hall.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
